<title>GERMANY: Gruner+Jahr 1995/96 profit falls to 242 mln DM.</title>
<headline>Gruner+Jahr 1995/96 profit falls to 242 mln DM.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   242     vs 376</p>
<p>    Group sales				  4,580   vs 4,380</p>
<p>    Group investments			  525     vs 921</p>
<p>    Group workforce			    12,594  vs 12,546</p>
<p>NOTE - German magazine publishing group Gruner+Jahr AG, a subsidiary of Bertelsmann AG, said its net results were burdened by a large addition to reserves for employee pensions. The operating profit was 560 million marks, slightly above last year's level, despite higher paper prices.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
